From 4da83d81204242edc3298a12783928d3a26fe88f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FiyeroT <me@fiyero.xyz>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 16:33:56 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 170/174] route: a chain with a URL test is dialed through the
 URL test

sing-box 1.14.4 resolves a group into the chain of outbounds a connection
goes through and dials the last of them. The URL test of podkop-engine judges
the dials of its members in its DialContext and ListenPacket: a member that
fails or does not answer is tested out of turn and left, a fallback is taken,
a member whose test is pending is not used. A dial past the group left all of
that out, and a dead member kept the new connections until the next test
round (3 minutes by default).

The chain stays for the metadata, the loop check and the interruption of the
connections; a connection is dialed through the first URL test of it, as
before 1.14.4. The history of a member is no longer deleted at any failed dial
of such a chain: the group tells a failure of the member from one of the
destination or of the network of the router.
